                    "about_opening_story": {
                      "type": "text",
                      "settings": {
                        "text": "<p>I was born and raised in Mexico. I trained there as an architect. I learned to see spaces before I entered them. How light moves through a room, how colours feel against each other, how the proportions of a composition either hold or fall apart. I thought I would spend my life doing that.</p><p>Los Angeles had other plans. My degree did not transfer. Ten years passed. I had a family, a home, a full life. And ten years without working. Without a place to put what was in my head.</p><p>Flowers were always part of my life. Bought at the market every week, loved simply. I never imagined they would become my profession, my therapy, and the place where I am most free.</p>",
                        "text_color": "",
                        "width": "100%",
                        "max_width": "none",
                        "alignment": "left",
                        "type_preset": "custom",
