            "about_roots": {
              "type": "text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p>Then 2020, and a family friend leaving Los Angeles with a small side business: Shabbat Flowers Club, Friday flower deliveries to the Jewish community, barely running, no real revenue. It came to me almost by accident. I was not looking for it.</p><p>The arrangements I walked into didn’t reflect how I see flowers. Everything in me said so. I have Polish Jewish roots—roots that travelled through Peru and into Mexico before landing in California. I understood what Friday means in a Jewish home. The flowers arriving at that table are not decoration. They are part of something. They needed to be right.</p>",
                "text_color": "",
                "width": "100%",
                "max_width": "none",
                "alignment": "left",
                "type_preset": "custom",
                "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
